  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \n   The proposed approach combines convex relaxation with a two-phase optimization strategy to find a good initial solution and then refine it for better performance.\n\n2. Mathematical specification  \n   The objective function to minimize is:\n   \n   \\[\n   C_5 = \\max_{k} \\sum_{i} h[i](1 - h[(i+k) \\mod n]) \\cdot dx\n   \\]\n   \n   Subject to:\n   \\[\n   0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1, \\quad \\sum h[i] = \\frac{n\\_points}{2}\n   \\]\n   \n   To handle the non-convexity, we first solve a relaxed version to minimize the sum of overlaps, then refine using gradient descent.\n\n3. Implementation procedure  \n   a. Use `initial_h_values` to initialize, ensuring feasibility.  \n   b. Solve a convex relaxation using CVXPY to minimize total overlap.  \n   c. Apply projected gradient descent on the solution, computing gradients with finite differences.  \n   d. Clip and rescale after each update to maintain constraints.  \n   e. Track best solution and terminate after 50 iterations without improvement.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations  \n   Use \\(n\\_points = 100\\). Set learning rate to 0.01, with decay every 100 iterations. Clip velocities for stability.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness  \n   Each iteration takes ~0.1s, allowing 1000 iterations within 600s. Include progress checks and fallback to the initial solution.\n\n6. Validation and return contract  \n   Ensure \\(h \\in [0,1]\\) and correct sum. Validate using the exact evaluator and return the best h and C\u2085.",
